  "section_notes": "The final text is strong on S1 (24-hour reporting, plus a one-time regulator-only reconciliation of prior unreported incidents) and S2 (5% cap with immediate sales stop, no public publication). It is comparatively lenient on S3, with a 6-year retrofit plan deadline that favours Northwind, and S4 is built-in suppression from 36 months, which favours Halcyon's cost position. S5 makes an 8-per-100k recall mandatory with no transition window, which is the most costly term for Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k). The customer-notice and results terms are unambiguous only as far as the wording allows; the S2 results clause ('results') is read as numeric rates, and the S3 6-year deadline is read as applying to the retrofit plan."
